From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 18:00:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] FlyWeb 3.2.0 interface: soft inner glow instead of the
 URL focus ring

From Titin's design (softmac FlyWeb/branding/interfaz-3.2.0): when the
URL field is focused, regular and guest windows show a soft gray inner
glow of about 2 dip instead of the colored focus ring. Private and Tor
windows keep Brave's focus ring.

The glow is a transparent child view added last, so it paints above the
omnibox textfield (which has an opaque background), and it is shown
under the same condition as Chromium's focus ring: caret visible and
popup closed. It is drawn with a few antialiased strokes that fade
inwards, without a blur filter. Thickness, color, opacity and steps are
constants (kFlyWebOmniboxFocusGlow*) to adjust in tests with Titin.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MwmK2juPkbC58kEi4QFeyU
